    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0533" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 850a.00/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-09T17:00:00+00:19"
                            >January 9, 1919—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 10—9:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>83. My 69, 4th. Note of December 31 referred to therein received today reiterates
                    the facts already communicated to you. The only difference being that the dates
                    of the abrogated conditions [<hi rendition="#italic">conventions?</hi>] are
                    cited, namely, November 11, 1902 and October 20, 25, 1865. Text follows by
                    pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
